# Ocelot Pride: "...for each token you control that entered this turn, create a token that's a copy of it." The copies are one
# instruction and enter together (CR 603.6a, 603.2c), so a creature that watches them sees every one enter. On turn 7 Bot1
# attacks with Ocelot Pride (life gained, before anything says players can't), then casts Ajani, Nacatl Pariah (its Cat Warrior
# token) and Rampaging Ferocidon ("Whenever another creature enters, it deals 1 damage to that creature's controller"), and
# Reflection of Kiki-Jiki makes a hasty token copy of the Ferocidon. At the end step the Pride makes a Cat (seen by the
# Ferocidon and its copy: 2 damage), then copies the Cat Warrior, the Ferocidon copy and the Cat at once: the Ferocidon sees 3
# enter, its first copy 3, and the new copy the 2 others (8). Copied one at a time the new Ferocidon would miss the Cat copy (7).
# Bot1: 20 + 1 lifelink - 1 (the copy of the Ferocidon entering) - 2 (the Cat) - 8 = 10.

